{"id": "EUVD-2026-103306", "enisaUuid": "20f6df0b-b28b-3c37-90c4-e4ba63d86f96", "description": "Admidio from 5.0.11 before 5.0.16 contains a broken access control vulnerability in modules/inventory/inventory_data.php that allows authenticated users to bypass the inventory_module_enabled restriction. Attackers with any valid login can request the DataTables JSON feed to read every inventory item and keeper names, even when the module is disabled.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:18:13", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Admidio/admidio/security/advisories/GHSA-5f29-r7rj-43mf", "https://github.com/Admidio/admidio/security/advisories/GHSA-qfjf-c48f-x87g", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/admidio-5.0.11-before-5.0.16-broken-access-control-via-inventory-data-php"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pf3j-3gfx-w49c", "CVE-2026-111914"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8ac19d52-3507-3bc4-9106-15cbf2a74e11", "product": {"name": "admidio", "vendor": {"name": "Admidio"}}, "product_version": "5.0.11 <5.0.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "53c6d035-d45e-3550-b35a-253944e699f4", "vendor": {"name": "Admidio"}}], "isExploited": false}